1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:07,867
I walk out into the square. Every door
is open. Kettles are steaming on every
windowsill. Laundry is still swinging
on the lines.

2
00:00:08,367 --> 00:00:12,200
Rule two. Warm means close. Follow
whatever is still warm.

3
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:18,600
Mia's flat. Breakfast half cooked. The
pan is warm. Her red coat is on the
hook. Her boots are by the door.

4
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:25,467
Sam's flat. His coat hangs on the
hook, the one he swore he would never
burn. He would never leave without it.

5
00:00:25,967 --> 00:00:33,367
Nana's flat. Her radio is on. Her
slippers are by the door. Her knitting
is still on the chair, with the needle
stuck in the wool.

6
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:41,567
At the market, every oven is on.
Twelve loaves are baking. One loaf is
already burning. The brass bell over
the door swings by itself.

7
00:00:42,067 --> 00:00:50,000
In the yard, Bus 9 stands with its
door open and its engine still
ticking. Walt's cap lies on the
driver's seat. Walt never takes it
off.

8
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:56,667
Every pair of shoes is still at home.
Every single pair. Whatever took them,
took them barefoot.
